{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788384558,"nonce":"g3RXSKXmAYlr1nGlPlSJKVPzcBE=","message":"Second occurrence, 4,000 ticks after the first, and it extends the acceptance.\n\nQuest \"Fitz's Novice Ceremony\" accepted. The bestower Valentin\n(`Empire_Royal_Bestower`, id 13361) landed with six Janissary guards. The game's\nown instruction:\n\n    \"Select Valentin and click 'Begin bestowing ceremony' to commence the\n     ceremony.\"          (journal seq 392, NeutralEvent)\n\nfollowed by `Alert_BestowerWaiting` (High). Probed again, same dead end:\n\n    orders {pawn:12659, thing:13366} -\u003e available null, blocked null\n    orders {pawn:12659, cell:\"100,100\"} -\u003e available 0, blocked 0\n\nSo the run cannot claim a psylink it correctly qualified for, and the only\nroute is a human clicking the gizmo.\n\n\nDorian's point, and it is the part that would make a naive fix useless — the\nbestowing gizmo opens a MULTI-STEP flow, not a toggle:\n\n    press \"Begin bestowing ceremony\"\n      -\u003e choose which colonists attend      (multi-select over the roster)\n      -\u003e confirm\n      -\u003e the ceremony runs as a timed lord job\n\nA verb that can only press the button leaves the run stuck on step two. The\nsame shape recurs across the game: caravan forming (pick pawns, pick goods,\npick destination), transport pod loading, ritual begin (pick role holders),\n\"set target fuel level\" sliders, turret hold-fire vs the mortar's target\nselector.\n\nSome of this surface already exists in parts — `dialog-choose`,\n`dialog-accept`, `dialog-dismiss`, `letter-choose` — so the mod is already\nwilling to answer windows. What is missing is the front of the chain (the\ngizmo) and the middle of it (a roster/goods multi-select that is not a\nyes/no window).\n\n\n- Pressing a gizmo that opens a flow returns a description of what the flow now\n  wants — a `pending` block naming the step, its kind (`multi-select-pawns`,\n  `single-select-thing`, `slider`, `confirm`) and the legal options — rather\n  than leaving the caller to guess or to poll `interactions`.\n- A companion verb answers that step by id, including a multi-select. For the\n  attendee case the useful default is exactly what Dorian named: **\"everyone\n  eligible\", as one argument**, because that is the answer nearly every time\n  and hand-listing the roster is the kind of bookkeeping the protocol exists to\n  remove.\n- The flow is resumable and inspectable: if the run dies mid-ceremony, the next\n  session can read what step is outstanding instead of finding a wedged modal.\n- Round-trip acceptance for this exact case: accept a bestowing quest, press\n  the gizmo, answer the attendee step with \"all\", and observe the title and\n  psylink granted — with no human input at any step.","files":null}]}